3I is responsible for:

1. Identity and authentication


2. Authorization


3. Least-authority enforcement


4. Scoped capability and action authority


5. Human approval and control


6. Emergency human control


7. Governance policies


8. Versioned and testable governance rules


9. Context-aware authority decisions


10. Sensitive-data protection


11. Secret management


12. Data-flow control


13. Tool security


14. Model security


15. Plugin/extension security


16. Resource security


17. Isolation and sandboxing


18. Blast-radius control


19. Security monitoring


20. Security events and incidents


21. Governance audit


22. Security provenance


23. Change authority


24. Deployment governance


25. Extension/plugin qualification


26. Cross-layer integration checking


27. System-wide invariant checking


28. Final integration acceptance


29. Release/deployment gates


30. Emergency security controls



3I governs how the ecosystem interacts safely.

It does not own every mechanism inside the ecosystem.


