Checker conclusion:

Material issue found in previous 3I boundary definition: YES

Correction required: YES

Correction integrated: YES

Original CNS architecture broken: NO

New subsystem required: NO

3J required: NO

Further structural change justified now: NO


Final decision:

> FREEZE 3I V1.1.



Any future change to 3I should now require implementation evidence, a demonstrated failure, a genuine security discovery, or another concrete engineering reason—not simply a desire to make the architecture more complicated.